    "notes": [
      "Push / Pull / Legs + Upper / Lower, five days: every muscle is trained about twice a week.",
      "Five days is the most this plan uses; Saturday is left free.",
      "Most sets are 6 to 15 reps, close to failure: the range that builds muscle.",
      "Extra sets for legs, and it is the last thing to be cut when time is short.",
      "Elbow: nothing that loads it is in the plan.",
      "Lower back: nothing risky for it is in the plan, and gentler options were picked first.",
      "No very heavy low-rep sets, and joint-friendly exercises first.",
      "Trimmed to fit 60 minutes: the most important lifts stayed.",
      "Nothing for biceps suits your elbow, so it is left out.",
      "Weights go up by themselves: reach the top of the rep range on every set and next time adds one step. Every 6th week is a lighter deload week."
    ]
  }
